<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
    <%- include('head', { title: 'Noir Mak', description: 'Noir Mak is the creative practice of Cam Mansanarez — a creative technologist and digital artist exploring queer identity, generative systems, glitch aesthetics, and live-coded performance. Portfolio, generative AI art, and exhibition archive.' }) %>

    <body>

        <%- include('header') %>

        <main>

            <!-- HERO SECTION -->
            <section id="hero">
                <div class="container">
                    <div class="hero-content">
                        <h1 class="visually-hidden">Noir Mak — Creative Technologist &amp; Digital Artist</h1>
                        <img src="./images/noirmak-logo-horizontal.png" alt="Noir Mak" class="hero-logo" width="1243" height="312">
                        <p class="hero-tagline">generative art &bull; immersive systems &bull; creative technology</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section><!-- END HERO -->

            <!-- FEATURED WORK SECTION -->
            <section id="featured">
                <div class="container">
                    <div class="row align-items-center">

                        <div class="col-lg-6">
                            <p class="featured-label">Featured Work</p>
                            <h2><%= featuredProject.name %></h2>
                            <p class="featured-description"><%= featuredProject.description %></p>
                            <a href="<%= featuredProject.url %>" class="hero-btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit <%= featuredProject.name %></a>
                        </div>

                        <div class="col-lg-6">
                            <img src="/images/<%= featuredProject.image %>" alt="<%= featuredProject.name %>" class="featured-img" width="1300" height="1264">
                            <div class="event-details">
                                <p class="shows-title">Live Coding + Generative Visuals by Noir Mak · Music &amp; Composition by Rayonism</p>
                                <p class="shows-meta">Friday, September 18, 2026 · 7:00 PM</p>
                                <p class="shows-meta">Big View Studio · 310 Willow Street, Fort Collins, CO</p>
                                <p class="shows-meta">After party: live DJ set by ruffknz, immediately following until 11 PM</p>
                                <p class="shows-meta">All ages · Free</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                    </div>
                </div>
            </section><!-- END FEATURED WORK -->

            <!-- REDACTED BODIES SECTION -->
            <section id="redacted-bodies">
                <div class="container">
                    <div class="row align-items-center">

                        <div class="col-lg-6">
                            <img src="./images/redacted-bodies-featured.png" alt="Redacted Bodies — generative artwork preview" class="featured-img" width="800" height="800">
                        </div>

                        <div class="col-lg-6">
                            <p class="featured-label">Generative Art</p>
                            <h2>Redacted Bodies</h2>
                            <p class="featured-description">A generative art project exploring queer identity, censorship, surveillance, and digital embodiment through a custom LoRA model trained on FLUX using a hand-curated dataset in ComfyUI.</p>
                            <a href="/collection" class="hero-btn">View the Project</a>
                        </div>

                    </div>
                </div>
            </section><!-- END REDACTED BODIES -->

            <!-- ABOUT SECTION -->
            <section id="about">
                <div class="container">
                    <div class="about-card">
                        <p class="featured-label">The Artist</p>
                        <h2 class="glitch-text">Cam Mansanarez / Noir Mak</h2>
                        <p class="about-text">Cam Mansanarez, known artistically as <strong>Noir Mak</strong>, is a creative technologist, digital artist, and creative coder whose work explores the evolving relationship between humans and computational systems. Based in Colorado, he designs generative artworks, immersive digital experiences, and interactive installations that blend artistic expression with technical innovation. His practice spans creative coding, live-coded visual performance, browser-based experiences, and experimental AI, using software as both a creative medium and a space for dialogue.</p>
                        <p class="about-text">Professionally, Cam specializes in translating emerging technologies into meaningful human experiences. Drawing from a background in customer success, product strategy, and creative technology, he approaches every project with equal attention to conceptual vision, technical execution, and user experience. Whether building a live performance system, training a custom AI model on a handmade dataset, or designing an interactive installation, his work is grounded in the belief that technology should deepen human connection rather than replace it.</p>
                        <p class="about-text">Working through a queer lens, Cam investigates how identity, memory, and representation evolve alongside computational systems. Rather than treating AI as a tool for automation, he approaches it as a creative collaborator, training intentionally curated, small-scale datasets to explore authorship, consent, and the expressive possibilities of human-machine collaboration.</p>
                        <p class="about-text">Cam has completed a Master's degree in Creative Technology, where his research focused on generative art, immersive media, interactive systems, and emerging technologies. His recent work includes live-coded visual performances using Hydra, browser-native generative experiences, custom-trained AI models, and computational artworks that merge code, data, poetry, and visual storytelling.</p>
                        <p class="about-text">Through Noir Mak, Cam creates work that exists between gallery, laboratory, and stage. He is passionate about collaborating with studios, cultural institutions, and forward-thinking organizations to design immersive experiences that are technically ambitious, visually compelling, and deeply human.</p>
                        <div class="text-center mt-4">
                            <a href="/contact" class="hero-btn">Contact the Artist</a>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section><!-- END ABOUT -->

            <!-- ARCHIVE SECTION -->
            <section id="archive">
                <div class="container">
                    <p class="featured-label">Archive</p>
                    <h2 class="section-title">The Archive</h2>
                    <% const accents = ['card-accent-1', 'card-accent-2', 'card-accent-3', 'card-accent-4']; %>
                    <div class="row g-4">

                        <% projectArray.forEach((item, index) => { %>
                        <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6 project-card-wrapper" style="--card-delay: <%= index * 0.08 %>s">
                            <div class="card project-card <%= accents[index % 4] %>">
                                <img src="/images/<%= item.image %>" class="card-img" alt="<%= item.name %>" width="800" height="560">
                                <div class="card-img-overlay d-flex align-items-end">
                                    <h5 class="project-title">
                                        <a href="/project/<%= item.id %>" class="stretched-link"><%= item.name %></a>
                                    </h5>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <% }) %>

                    </div><!-- END ROW -->
                </div><!-- END CONTAINER -->
            </section><!-- END ARCHIVE -->

            <!-- LIVE CODING SECTION -->
            <section id="live-coding">
                <div class="container">

                    <p class="featured-label">Live Performance</p>
                    <h2 class="section-title">Live Coding</h2>

                    <!-- Description + Featured Video -->
                    <div class="row align-items-center mb-5">

                        <div class="col-lg-6">
                            <p class="live-coding-text">Cam performs live using hand-coded visuals built in Hydra Video Synth — a browser-based, JavaScript/WebGL live coding environment for real-time visual composition. His performances are fully audio-reactive, responding to sound in real time to produce immersive, glitch-driven visual landscapes that exist only in the moment of performance.</p>
                            <p class="live-coding-text">Signal Bloom is his capstone project: a modular AI-assisted live visual performance environment merging Hydra live coding, generative AI imagery using ComfyUI, and audio-reactive systems into a unified performance instrument. The work investigates the evolving relationship between performer, machine, and emergence.</p>
                            <a href="https://github.com/cmansanarez/Signal_Bloom/blob/main/README.md" class="hero-btn" target="_blank">Work In Progress - View Signal Bloom Repo</a>
                        </div>

                        <div class="col-lg-6">
                            <div class="video-embed">
                                <div class="ratio ratio-16x9">
                                    <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/zqkRFfcOIhc" title="Live Coding Performance — Noir Mak" allowfullscreen></iframe>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                    </div><!-- END ROW -->

                    <!-- Performance Image Gallery -->
                    <div class="row g-3">
                        <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6 gallery-accent-blue">
                            <img src="./images/noirmak-website-livcoding-left.jpg" class="live-gallery-img" alt="Live Coding Performance" width="800" height="500">
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6 gallery-accent-yellow">
                            <img src="./images/noirmak-website-livcoding-center.jpg" class="live-gallery-img" alt="Live Coding Performance" width="800" height="500">
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6 gallery-accent-green">
                            <img src="./images/noirmak-website-livcoding-right.jpg" class="live-gallery-img" alt="Live Coding Performance" width="800" height="500">
                        </div>
                    </div><!-- END GALLERY ROW -->

                </div><!-- END CONTAINER -->
            </section><!-- END LIVE CODING -->

            <!-- SHOWS SECTION -->
            <section id="shows">
                <div class="container">

                    <p class="featured-label">Exhibitions & Performances</p>
                    <h2 class="section-title">Shows</h2>

                    <div class="shows-timeline">

                        <!-- 2026 -->
                        <div class="shows-year-group">
                            <div class="shows-year-heading">
                                <div class="shows-year-dot"></div>
                                <span class="shows-year">2026</span>
                            </div>

                            <div class="shows-entry">
                                <p class="shows-title">Signal Bloom — with Rayonism</p>
                                <p class="shows-meta">Live Coding, Generative Visuals & Modular Synth · Big View Studio, Fort Collins, CO</p>
                                <p class="shows-meta">Music & composition by Rayonism · after party DJ set by ruffknz</p>
                                <p class="shows-meta">September 18, 2026</p>
                            </div>
                            <hr class="shows-divider">

                            <div class="shows-entry">
                                <p class="shows-title">Live Coding Visuals</p>
                                <p class="shows-meta">Drone Show · The DMV, Denver, CO</p>
                                <p class="shows-meta">August 20, 2026</p>
                            </div>
                            <hr class="shows-divider">

                            <div class="shows-entry">
                                <p class="shows-title">Live Coding Visuals</p>
                                <p class="shows-meta">NoCo Noise Floor No. 43 · Museum of Art Fort Collins, CO</p>
                                <p class="shows-meta">August 15, 2026</p>
                            </div>
                            <hr class="shows-divider">

                            <div class="shows-entry">
                                <p class="shows-title">Signal Bloom — First Fridays at Big View Studio</p>
                                <p class="shows-meta">Live Coding, Generative Systems & AI Visuals · Big View Studio, Fort Collins, CO</p>
                                <p class="shows-meta">Dual exhibition with Seeing Sound by Sam Wheeler</p>
                                <p class="shows-meta">July 3, 2026</p>
                            </div>
                            <hr class="shows-divider">

                            <div class="shows-entry">
                                <p class="shows-title"><a href="https://focofringe.org/events/nimby-co-80443/" target="_blank">"NIMBy, CO 80443" — FoCo Fringe Festival</a></p>
                                <p class="shows-meta">Live Coding & Generative Visuals · Sound Bar Alley Stage, Fort Collins, CO</p>
                                <p class="shows-meta">Night 1: Generative visuals · Night 2: Live coding</p>
                                <p class="shows-meta">June 12–13, 2026</p>
                            </div>
                            <hr class="shows-divider">

                            <div class="shows-entry">
                                <p class="shows-title"><a href="https://visit-lumyn.noirmak.com/" target="_blank">"Lumyn: Constellation of Self"</a></p>
